1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
That tire light in August

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
might be heat, not a warning.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Air expands with heat —
about 1 PSI every 10 degrees.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Drive on hot asphalt
and your reading climbs.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Check it hot midday
and it looks fine.

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Check it cold next morning —
it can read several PSI low.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Underinflated on a hot highway

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
is exactly when a tire
is most likely to overheat.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Check pressure cold,
before you drive.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Or stop by — Nick's Tire
and Auto, link in bio.
